@page "/"
<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<style>
    /* A flex container to hold the side videos and the center content */
    .page-container {
        display: flex;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100vh; /* Full viewport height */
        overflow: hidden;
    }
    /* Style for the side video sections */
    .side-video {
        flex: 1;
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

        .side-video video {
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            object-fit: cover;
        }
    /* Central content container styling */
    .content {
        flex: 0 0 800px; /* Fixed width for the content */
        /* background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6); /* Semi-transparent background for readability */ 
        background: #280acaa3;
        color: #fff;
        padding: 2rem;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        text-align: left;
        overflow-y: auto;
    }
</style>

<div class="page-container">
    <!-- Left side video -->
    <div class="side-video">
        <video autoplay muted loop>
            <source src="videos/cryptographyvideo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
            Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
    </div>

    <!-- Center content -->
    <div class="content">
        <h1 class="display-4">Welcome to SecureChat!</h1>
        <p class="lead">Exploring Cryptography and Its Techniques</p>

        <h3>What is Cryptography?</h3>
        <p>
            Cryptography is the science of protecting information by transforming it into an unreadable format.
            It is essential in keeping digital communication secure and private.
        </p>

        <h4>Cryptographic Techniques</h4>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Caesar Cipher:</strong> A substitution cipher that shifts letters by a fixed number.</li>
            <li><strong>Monoalphabetic Cipher:</strong> Replaces each letter with a fixed substitution throughout the message.</li>
            <li><strong>Polyalphabetic Cipher:</strong> Uses multiple substitution alphabets to encrypt the text (e.g., Vigenère cipher).</li>
            <li><strong>Hill Cipher:</strong> Uses linear algebra and matrix multiplication for encryption.</li>
            <li><strong>Playfair Cipher:</strong> Encrypts digraphs (pairs of letters) using a 5x5 key square.</li>
            <li><strong>One-Time Pad (OTP):</strong> A theoretically unbreakable cipher using a random key that’s as long as the message.</li>
            <li><strong>Rail Fence Cipher:</strong> A transposition cipher that writes text in a zigzag pattern on rails.</li>
            <li><strong>Columnar Transposition:</strong> Rearranges the characters of plaintext into columns using a keyword.</li>
            <li><strong>DES (Data Encryption Standard):</strong> A symmetric-key algorithm for the encryption of digital data.</li>
            <li><strong>AES (Advanced Encryption Standard):</strong> A widely used secure symmetric block cipher.</li>
            <li><strong>RC4:</strong> A stream cipher using variable-length keys and fast encryption/decryption.</li>
            <li><strong>RSA:</strong> A public-key encryption technique based on the difficulty of factoring large integers.</li>
            <li><strong>ECC (Elliptic Curve Cryptography):</strong> Uses elliptic curves for secure public-key cryptography.</li>
            <li><strong>Diffie-Hellman (DH) Key Exchange:</strong> A method of securely exchanging cryptographic keys over a public channel.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Right side video -->
    <div class="side-video">
        <video autoplay muted loop>
            <source src="videos/cryptographyvideo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
            Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
    </div>
</div>
